WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.450
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann.

00:00:02.009 --> 00:00:05.310
Today I want to talk about how
to choose a language to learn.

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.360
Now, if you enjoy these videos,
please subscribe, click on

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.120
the bell for notifications.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:17.220
If you follow this on podcasts,
Apple Podcasts, or Spotify or

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.460
elsewhere, um, please leave a review.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.390
It's always appreciated.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:26.655
Know how to choose the language to learn.

00:00:26.775 --> 00:00:30.315
Well, first of all, you know, this is to
me, a very interesting subject because

00:00:30.555 --> 00:00:35.325
most people who are learning a language
didn't really choose that language.

00:00:36.015 --> 00:00:40.845
I start with the situation in
Canada where it's, because Canada

00:00:40.845 --> 00:00:42.075
has two official languages.

00:00:42.555 --> 00:00:46.335
If you are in the French language
system, you're going to learn English.

00:00:46.365 --> 00:00:48.555
And if you're in the English
language, school system,

00:00:48.585 --> 00:00:49.515
you're going to learn French.

00:00:50.055 --> 00:00:53.325
Uh, how motivated are the kids to learn?

00:00:53.325 --> 00:00:54.745
Did they choose those languages?

00:00:55.485 --> 00:01:00.135
I think that in reality, probably
the kids in the French school system

00:01:00.345 --> 00:01:04.875
are more motivated to learn English
than vice versa, because English

00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:10.215
is so much more important than the
North American context than French.

00:01:10.935 --> 00:01:14.055
Kids in the French, in the English
language, school system are not

00:01:14.055 --> 00:01:16.695
tremendously motivated to learn
French, which is a big reason

00:01:16.695 --> 00:01:18.195
why they don't do very well.

00:01:18.785 --> 00:01:22.605
If you live in the United States,
probably Spanish is the language that

00:01:22.605 --> 00:01:25.455
you're most often asked to learn.

00:01:25.905 --> 00:01:30.765
So the first thing I would say is that if
the language learner has the opportunity

00:01:30.765 --> 00:01:35.475
to choose the language to learn, there's a
greater likelihood that they will do well.

00:01:35.775 --> 00:01:36.705
So that's number one.

00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:40.875
So I have always said, or have often
said that it's unfortunate that

00:01:40.905 --> 00:01:44.535
let's say in Canada, kids are told
to learn French, that it's their

00:01:44.535 --> 00:01:47.565
obligation to learn French somehow,
because it's an official language.

00:01:48.265 --> 00:01:53.145
If they had the choice to learn whatever
language they wanted and if they were

00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:57.885
then able to learn that language, they
will subsequently always be able to

00:01:57.885 --> 00:02:01.575
learn French because once you have
learned one language, you have the

00:02:01.575 --> 00:02:05.625
confidence, you know how to do it and
your brain is a little more flexible.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:09.195
You're going to find it easier to
learn another language by and large.

00:02:09.405 --> 00:02:14.775
So I think in our schools, we would
be better to give the kids a choice.

00:02:14.925 --> 00:02:18.615
Now it used to be that, you know,
if a school doesn't have, like, you

00:02:18.615 --> 00:02:21.795
can't give the kids the choice of
any of 10 languages, because then

00:02:21.795 --> 00:02:24.834
we would need to have teachers of
each of those 10 languages and the

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:28.155
schools can't afford to carry teachers
of all these different languages.

00:02:28.424 --> 00:02:33.225
That's no longer a factor because
nowadays there are so many language

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:38.475
learning resources available on
the web, including teachers online,

00:02:38.475 --> 00:02:40.845
including, uh, audio books and movies.

00:02:40.845 --> 00:02:45.614
And, uh, you name it, LingQ of
course, that if the schools had the

00:02:45.614 --> 00:02:50.234
teachers who were knowledgeable about
how to learn languages, uh, via the

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:52.185
internet, that's all they would need.

00:02:52.185 --> 00:02:55.185
They wouldn't need to have specific
teachers for each language.

00:02:55.394 --> 00:02:57.765
They can even find those teachers online.

00:02:57.945 --> 00:03:03.075
So it would be great if in schools,
people were given the choice.

00:03:03.165 --> 00:03:07.035
Now, assuming we have the choice,
which language should we learn now?

00:03:07.214 --> 00:03:11.645
The next, so my whole thing about language
learning is get rid of the obligations.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:15.540
So the first sort of obligation is
the school system says you shall

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.490
learn English or French or Spanish or
whatever the case might be and give

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:21.870
people choice, give the kids choice.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:28.140
Second of all, very often, uh, parents
of immigrants are very keen that

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:32.820
their children should learn the call
it ancestral language, sometimes

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.530
called the heritage language.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:35.940
I'm also against that.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:42.405
If that works, if the parents speak with
the kids around the house in that language

00:03:42.405 --> 00:03:44.295
and the kids pick it up, that's great.

00:03:44.295 --> 00:03:48.855
Or if our grandparents live together
with the kids and they speak the language

00:03:48.855 --> 00:03:49.875
and they pick it up, that's great.

00:03:49.965 --> 00:03:54.375
But if that's not the situation,
uh, I'm not tremendously in favor of

00:03:54.395 --> 00:03:58.865
sending the kids to Chinese school or
Russian school or, you know, Persian

00:03:58.865 --> 00:04:03.565
school, uh, to learn that ancestral
language, unless the kids are interested.

00:04:03.975 --> 00:04:07.985
Uh, it may be that the kid whose,
whose family was Chinese speaking

00:04:08.005 --> 00:04:11.505
might be more interested in
Spanish or some other language.

00:04:11.775 --> 00:04:15.825
And so always, I favor the idea of
letting people choose the language

00:04:15.825 --> 00:04:17.295
that they are most interested in.

00:04:17.655 --> 00:04:19.995
So then how do you choose
which language to learn?

00:04:20.025 --> 00:04:22.605
People are going to be more
successful if they're motivated.

00:04:22.605 --> 00:04:28.155
So, you know, if you feel a tremendous
interest in the culture of a particular

00:04:28.155 --> 00:04:32.940
country, If you have relatives because
you come from a certain country and you

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:37.620
want to communicate with those relatives,
uh, if, uh, you saw a movie, if you're

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:43.320
interested in anime, in other words,
wherever you have a motivation, uh,

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:44.729
that's the language you should learn.

00:04:45.479 --> 00:04:50.070
Uh, even if it theoretically
is hard, uh, it doesn't matter.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:54.300
You should go for the language you're most
motivated to learn because that motivation

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.969
will carry you through the difficulties.

00:04:57.510 --> 00:05:01.260
Uh, and as I said, in other videos,
you know, the initial period is you're

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.969
learning few, you know, new words.

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:06.900
You're able to understand some things,
but the path to sort of genuine,

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.830
comfortable communication in the
language, you know, is a long one.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:15.600
And therefore you need to have this,
this motivation to sustain you.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:21.495
So I would very much favor learning a
language you're very interested in over

00:05:21.495 --> 00:05:25.935
one that you think might be more useful
because once you've learned one language,

00:05:25.935 --> 00:05:27.705
it's easier to learn another language.

00:05:27.825 --> 00:05:31.935
So go for the one that you're likely
to succeed in, and you're more

00:05:31.935 --> 00:05:35.685
likely to succeed in the language
that you're very motivated to learn.

00:05:36.315 --> 00:05:36.825
Okay.

00:05:37.245 --> 00:05:42.225
Um, other considerations, obviously,
if you know related languages, if you

00:05:42.225 --> 00:05:46.335
know a related language, if you know
Spanish, you might want to go for...

00:05:46.915 --> 00:05:51.750
spanish or French or Portuguese or
Italian, because obviously if you

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:55.890
have success again, that's going
to encourage you to continue or

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:57.360
at the very least to stay with it.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:00.150
So I have tended to want to do that.

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:01.020
I learned Russian.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:04.770
Then I went from, uh, Czech and
then Ukrainian and then Polish.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.100
And because I knew Spanish, I wanted
to learn Portuguese and Italian,

00:06:08.219 --> 00:06:10.530
the so-called low hanging fruit.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:14.820
So, uh, obviously we, we like to push
where there's the least resistance.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:19.020
One consideration is your
degree of motivation, obviously.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:22.500
And I think that's the that's
paramount, but another consideration

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:25.710
is how easy is it going to be
for you to learn that language?

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:29.670
Now, if you are not interested in
the language, even if theoretically

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:32.430
it's easier, you're going to
have a tough time learning it.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:37.200
Because I repeat in my experience,
motivation is the biggest consideration,

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:42.810
uh, in choosing a language, um, Obviously
the things that make it easier could

00:06:42.810 --> 00:06:44.430
also include the writing system.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.640
You really have to commit to
learn a language where the

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:48.840
writing system is different.

00:06:49.409 --> 00:06:53.400
Uh, it's a lot tougher because reading
is such a big part of language learning.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:57.390
And when we're dealing with a different
writing system, even if we learn what

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.870
the characters represent and so forth,
it's always harder for the brain

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:03.330
to, to read in a different script.

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:04.530
At least that's been my approach.

00:07:05.475 --> 00:07:10.485
Uh, because if I spent 75 years, not
75, but if I spent most of my life

00:07:10.485 --> 00:07:14.474
reading in the Latin alphabet, my brain
is very used to the Latin alphabet.

00:07:14.804 --> 00:07:19.455
No, no matter how well I can read in
Chinese or Korean or Japanese or Russian,

00:07:19.665 --> 00:07:24.105
I will never feel as comfortable in those
alphabets as I do in my own alphabet.

00:07:24.165 --> 00:07:25.575
And the same is true in reverse.

00:07:25.575 --> 00:07:31.075
If you are a Japanese reader, speaker,
or a Persian speaker or Chinese or

00:07:31.094 --> 00:07:34.815
Russian, then you're always going to
be more comfortable I think in the

00:07:34.815 --> 00:07:38.925
language, in the writing system that
you've spent most of your life reading.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:44.219
So motivation is number one, but
then how difficult is it going to be?

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.770
And so there is this tendency
to want to go for something

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:50.060
that's, you know, um, easier.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:55.310
Now I should, one final thing, and,
and this is probably what ends up

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:59.150
being the main reason why people learn
a given language, you know, in the

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:01.669
real world is because it's useful.

00:08:02.565 --> 00:08:07.395
So, you know, English tends to be
the language that's, uh, studied the

00:08:07.395 --> 00:08:11.265
most around the world because it's
been perceived to be the most useful.

00:08:11.775 --> 00:08:15.195
Uh, now there are people who say
Chinese is going to be useful

00:08:15.195 --> 00:08:19.455
because it's such a huge country
with a, you know, huge economy.

00:08:19.844 --> 00:08:26.565
Uh, so that's, uh, you know, if you
consider that to be useful, but if you

00:08:26.565 --> 00:08:30.195
are a, if you want to work in Germany
or you want to work in Japan, or you

00:08:30.195 --> 00:08:34.590
want to work in Brazil, then there
are reasons why in those scenarios,

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:39.480
those languages or in other similar
situations, wouldn't be the most useful.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:42.420
So usefulness obviously is a big factor.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:46.530
Uh, but if, if you find that, that if you
are convinced that that language is going

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:50.460
to be useful, but you're not genuinely
motivated to learn it because you don't

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.160
like it, you may find it difficult.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:57.990
So in an ideal scenario,
you can combine the useful.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.530
Things that motivate you.

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:06.540
If you can combine the usefulness
and, and, and pleasure, you

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.189
have the best of both worlds.

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:13.050
And particularly if the language is,
you know, if you're an English speaking

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:16.530
person learning French or Spanish,
it's written in the same alphabet.

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:18.750
A lot of the vocabulary is in common.

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:23.250
Actually, if you are combining
pleasure with use utility and

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.949
it's not too difficult, you
should have an easy time of it.

00:09:27.675 --> 00:09:29.445
Right now I'm learning Persian and Arabic.

00:09:29.475 --> 00:09:30.405
I've learned Chinese.

00:09:30.405 --> 00:09:31.365
I've learned Russian.

00:09:31.365 --> 00:09:33.405
I've learned, uh, Japanese.

00:09:33.555 --> 00:09:38.265
So if you are motivated enough, you
will overcome all the other obstacles.

00:09:38.325 --> 00:09:42.725
So I hope that's helpful in how to
choose the language to study, to learn.

00:09:43.215 --> 00:09:43.845
Thanks for listening.

